<title>USA: Niagara Mohawk seeks rate proceeding delay.</title>
<headline>Niagara Mohawk seeks rate proceeding delay.</headline>
<dateline>SYRACUSE, N.Y. 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Niagara Mohawk Power Corp said Friday it had asked that its 1997 rate proceeding be put on indefinite hold while the utility moves toward finalizing its agreement with 19 independent power producers and completes PowerChoice negotiations.</p>
<p>In a filing Friday with the state Public Service Commission, the company said it can withdraw its rate request entirely after financing for the agreement and PowerChoice are completed.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.))</p>
